Root cause: TrustedCertificates.CurrentlyValidTrustManager implements plain X509TrustManager, not X509ExtendedTrustManager, so SSLContextImpl wraps it in AbstractTrustManagerWrapper, whose checkAlgorithmConstraints runs over the whole PRESENTED chain (minus a trailing getAcceptedIssuers() member), not over the path the platform validated. A backend presenting a valid [leaf, given CA] path followed by an extra certificate the path does not need, if that extra certificate has a legacy signature (MD5withRSA here), is rejected with 502 CONNECT_FAILED under trustCertificates(ca), while the platform trust manager over the same CA (an X509ExtendedTrustManager, not wrapped) accepts it. This also makes docs/api/proxy.md and docs/api/en/proxy.md false where they say extra certificates the path does not need have no effect whether the backend sends them (FR-PROXY-022 AC-7).
